{
  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a charity campaigner and Paralympian-style endurance athlete who became paralysed in a 2007 riding accident, has died at 44 after an accident in Jordan. Known for completing the 2012 London Marathon over 17 days in a bionic suit and for raising nearly £1 million for charity, she inspired many through later events including the Great North Run while pregnant. Her family asked for privacy as they grieve."
}

